    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Backtest Ops alert rules",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "id": 131,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Three alert rules are committed with this dashboard; **live wiring (contact points / thresholds) is M10 observability work** (per plan §12).\n\n1. **Queue wait p95 > 10 min** — `histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(backtest_queue_wait_seconds_bucket[30m]))) > 600`. Fires when runs are waiting more than 10 minutes to start — the classic symptom of the `worker-backtest` service not being provisioned or not keeping up. See `docs/runbooks/backtest-stuck.md` §1.\n2. **Any run hits the hard time cap** — `increase(backtest_failed_total{reason=\"BACKTEST_TIME_CAP\"}[10m]) > 0`. A run exceeded the 25-min soft limit (hard kill at 30 min). Not an outage — the job was too big for the budget; shrink the grid / range / symbols. Runbook §5.\n3. **Failed-rate > 20% over 1h** — `sum(increase(backtest_failed_total[1h])) / clamp_min(sum(increase(backtest_runs_total[1h])), 1) > 0.2`. A broad failure spike — check `backtest_failed_total{reason}` to localize (time cap vs insufficient-data vs engine error). Runbook §6."
      }
    }
